  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only multiprofile with PCA and avgpool is the best current setup (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), while transformer aggregation and scGPT are weaker, and image-only ResNet is very weak (0.208 accuracy). The key uncertainty is whether adding image information to the proven RNA setup can improve validation accuracy. config_018 keeps the best known RNA representation, profile, and aggregation fixed while adding ResNet image features with simple concat fusion, directly testing whether multimodal fusion helps under the current strongest baseline. This is the best next use of budget because it exploits the strongest evidence while clarifying whether image modality is worth further exploration before trying more complex ViT or weighted-fusion variants."
